      en: "Rubud al Gharbiyya (West Rubud) is a 0.2 km² islet in the Rubud group, the smallest, composed of sand and shell debris. Uninhabited, it is occasionally visited by fishermen. The surrounding shallow waters host mantis shrimp and bivalves. The islet is surrounded by tidal channels and lies 2 km offshore from Askar. It has no vegetation and is subject to strong tidal currents. The area is part of a proposed marine reserve.",
